1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,959
This tutorial follows a tenancy contract
that ended

2
00:00:03,959 --> 00:00:07,424
early, from termination to the deposit
refund.

3
00:00:07,424 --> 00:00:11,878
As the Accountant, open Grace Okafor's
contract for R-203:

4
00:00:11,878 --> 00:00:16,333
70,000 of rent a year from 15 October
2025.

5
00:00:16,333 --> 00:00:20,292
She relocated and left on 31 May 2026.

6
00:00:20,292 --> 00:00:25,736
The contract is Closed, and its settlement
summary shows the 3,500

7
00:00:25,736 --> 00:00:30,686
deposit held, 750 of deductions and a
refund of 11,332.19.

8
00:00:30,686 --> 00:00:32,665
Open the Cheques tab.

9
00:00:32,665 --> 00:00:34,645
Three rent cheques cleared.

10
00:00:34,645 --> 00:00:38,110
The July cheque was dated after she

11
00:00:38,110 --> 00:00:41,574
left, so termination returned it to her.

12
00:00:41,574 --> 00:00:46,029
In the Rent Receivable ledger below, the
reversal of

13
00:00:46,029 --> 00:00:50,483
its post-dated cheque journal debits Rent
Receivable with 17,500.

14
00:00:50,483 --> 00:00:54,937
Termination also wrote a TCR journal: the
rent after

15
00:00:54,937 --> 00:00:58,897
31 May was never earned, so Advance Rent

16
00:00:58,897 --> 00:01:02,856
is debited and Rent Receivable credited
with 26,082.19.

17
00:01:02,856 --> 00:01:06,321
The balance ends at 8,582.19 in credit,

18
00:01:06,321 --> 00:01:09,785
because Grace paid more than she used.

19
00:01:09,785 --> 00:01:11,765
Now open the settlement.

20
00:01:11,765 --> 00:01:16,219
The statement is computed from the ledger:
earned rent

21
00:01:16,219 --> 00:01:20,674
43,917.81, received 56,000 with the
deposit, a receivable balance

22
00:01:20,674 --> 00:01:24,633
of minus 8,582.19, and 3,500 of deposit
held.

23
00:01:24,633 --> 00:01:30,077
Move-out cleaning of 750 is deducted, so
the refund to Grace

24
00:01:30,077 --> 00:01:35,027
is 11,332.19, and it has been paid, with
nothing outstanding.

25
00:01:35,027 --> 00:01:37,501
Open the settlement journal, STL.

26
00:01:37,501 --> 00:01:42,946
It debits Security Deposit with 3,500 and
Rent Receivable with 8,582.19,

27
00:01:42,946 --> 00:01:48,390
and credits Maintenance Charges with 750
and Refunds payable with 11,332.19.

28
00:01:48,390 --> 00:01:52,844
Until it is paid, the refund is a
liability.

29
00:01:52,844 --> 00:01:56,804
It was paid by transfer five days later.

30
00:01:56,804 --> 00:02:01,258
In Journal Voucher, the payment voucher
BPV debits Refunds

31
00:02:01,258 --> 00:02:05,713
payable and credits the Emirates Islamic
account for the

32
00:02:05,713 --> 00:02:09,672
Residences with 11,332.19, and the
liability is cleared.
